- Real DOM vs Virtual DOM      

The Real DOM is the live, browser-rendered structure of a web page, while the Virtual DOM is a lightweight, in-memory JavaScript copy of that structure used by frameworks like React.
 The Real DOM updates elements directly in the browser. The Virtual DOM updates a JavaScript copy first, compares the changes using a diffing algorithm, and then applies only the necessary minimum changes to the Real DOM 
 In real DOM Even minor changes require traversing the entire DOM tree, which affects performance.
